WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:13.360
 Abby's many years of service required him to come up now. I appreciate it. What

00:00:13.360 --> 00:00:16.000
 is his son Michael now?

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:22.380
 He's the vice president of analytics and portfolio management at PNC Financial.

00:00:22.380 --> 00:00:24.000
 Michael Kamana.

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:40.860
 And he's also a speculative fiction author. The other is Pierre DeGionne.

00:00:40.860 --> 00:00:41.800
 Pierre is the publisher of Profile News, which is the largest Arabic English

00:00:41.800 --> 00:00:44.000
 newspaper in all of Ohio.

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:53.000
 That's huge. He's also Abby's successor as president of Cameo and other groups.

00:00:53.000 --> 00:00:58.000
 It's my pleasure to introduce first, Pierre DeGionne.

00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:13.980
 I hope you're having a great time. I think we have a great lineup here tonight.

00:01:13.980 --> 00:01:14.000
 And I really want to thank the bottom of my heart, the Hansin family. Let's

00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:14.000
 give them a big hand of applause.

00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:21.590
 Thank you so much for what you do to the international community. Thank you so

00:01:21.590 --> 00:01:28.360
 much for this international hall of fame. You guys are a legendary in our

00:01:28.360 --> 00:01:33.000
 community and God bless you for being involved so much.

00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:40.150
 My name is Pierre DeGionne, as you have mentioned. And I am the president of

00:01:40.150 --> 00:01:46.000
 the Cleveland American Police Organization, known as Cameo.

00:01:46.000 --> 00:01:52.260
 And the chairman of the board of the American Lebanese Community Council and

00:01:52.260 --> 00:01:59.290
 the Lebanese Cultural Guard. Also, we are affiliated with the world Lebanese

00:01:59.290 --> 00:02:01.000
 Cultural Union.

00:02:01.000 --> 00:02:09.420
 I want to congratulate our dear friends inducted here tonight. They mean so

00:02:09.420 --> 00:02:16.000
 much to us. Judge of Purdue Junior, Rocky. Congratulations.

00:02:16.000 --> 00:02:22.550
 And Sheila Crawford, the president of the House of the Guard. Thank you for

00:02:22.550 --> 00:02:25.000
 what you've done.

00:02:25.000 --> 00:02:33.610
 What I'm going to do is to be here inducting you, the leader, the philanthropist

00:02:33.610 --> 00:02:36.000
 in the Lebanese community.

00:02:36.000 --> 00:02:42.490
 Abby, as we say in Arabic, Abdulla, Meena. Abby grew up in Kefraya, 11 in the

00:02:42.490 --> 00:02:52.740
 town located in the Bikar Valley. He was one of 10 siblings, came to the US in

00:02:52.740 --> 00:02:59.000
 1956, and issued a living in Richmond, Virginia, where he attended college.

00:02:59.000 --> 00:03:07.000
 And then, thank you to his lovely wife, Mona. She pursued him to relocate to Kefraya.

00:03:07.000 --> 00:03:13.000
 Thank you, Mona.

00:03:13.000 --> 00:03:19.800
 Abby is a clerk, not only to the Lebanese community, but to the whole of the

00:03:19.800 --> 00:03:22.000
 Eastern community.

00:03:22.000 --> 00:03:30.560
 There are not enough words to describe this Greek man. It will take me forever

00:03:30.560 --> 00:03:32.000
 to talk about him.

00:03:32.000 --> 00:03:41.320
 But I will alleviate as much as I can because I have to do it so. He's humble,

00:03:41.320 --> 00:03:50.300
 gentle, kind, a man of knowledge, help, peace, and constantly striving for

00:03:50.300 --> 00:03:51.000
 harmony in the community.

00:03:51.000 --> 00:04:03.000
 I have known Abby for over 30 years. My first meeting with him was in Kenya.

00:04:03.000 --> 00:04:11.000
 Abby was the longest serving president of Kenya, serving over 15 years.

00:04:11.000 --> 00:04:21.090
 He has remained very much involved as a board member and a parliamentarian. He

00:04:21.090 --> 00:04:23.000
 was also a former president of the Kirby Club.

00:04:23.000 --> 00:04:29.940
 It's an Lebanese club in northern Ohio. Abby remained active in our Lebanese

00:04:29.940 --> 00:04:36.100
 community, currently serving as a vice chairman and a board member of the

00:04:36.100 --> 00:04:40.000
 American Lebanese Community Council and the Lebanese Cultural Authority.

00:04:40.000 --> 00:04:46.180
 He is a devoted member of St Elias Milkeit Catholic Church, located in the

00:04:46.180 --> 00:04:51.000
 Brooklyn, where he served as a president of the council.

00:04:51.000 --> 00:04:58.530
 Abby recently retired from his weekly Arabic radio broadcasting show, which was

00:04:58.530 --> 00:05:02.000
 featured on WCSB for 21 years.

00:05:02.000 --> 00:05:09.590
 Abby has selfishly served the community for decades, helping hundreds of people

00:05:09.590 --> 00:05:15.000
 with immigration paperwork and translation services.

00:05:15.000 --> 00:05:24.640
 His involvement turns so deep into the community, as he has helped countless

00:05:24.640 --> 00:05:34.580
 people facilitate the process of coming to the US, finding them employment and

00:05:34.580 --> 00:05:40.000
 transforming people from the old country,

00:05:40.000 --> 00:05:47.430
 and assimilating them to life in the United States of America. He is a friend,

00:05:47.430 --> 00:05:54.000
 a mentor, and confident, not only to me, but to countless others.

00:05:54.000 --> 00:06:00.950
 Abby has been married to his wife Mona for 55 years. They have two children,

00:06:00.950 --> 00:06:06.000
 Michael and Sarah, and Dorothy, and three grandchildren.

00:06:06.000 --> 00:06:13.810
 Abby, you are one of the special select few in the Cleveland community to be

00:06:13.810 --> 00:06:20.000
 chosen as an inductee to the International Hall of Fame.

00:06:20.000 --> 00:06:29.000
 You are an example. We all strive to emulate. Congratulations on your induction.

00:06:29.000 --> 00:06:33.000
 I present you, Abby Wiener. Thank you.

00:06:36.000 --> 00:06:43.000
 Thank you.

